        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/dougherty-tx-rains-county",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community’s cemetery, donated by Dougherty’s son in 1877, earned a Texas Historical Marker in 1980.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/dougherty-tx-rains-county",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A historic home built in 1880 served as a gathering place and later the headquarters of Dougherty Rural Telephone Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/dougherty-tx-rains-county",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Dougherty sits at the junction of Farm Roads 275 and 514, about six miles north of Emory in northern Rains County.",
